			"text": "PROTOBUF",
			"rawText": "PROTOBUF",
			"fontSize": 16.063917631513828,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "center",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "d3n3QwLkl9b2hn9t3xQaQ",
			"originalText": "PROTOBUF",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25
		},
		{
			"id": "8PgqQHGs",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 7189.554329865911,
			"y": 555.1065725394371,
			"width": 1096.592041015625,
			"height": 180.71907335453056,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bDI",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1813424951,
			"version": 1214,
			"versionNonce": 1859220953,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773092895283,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Thrift, Protobuf:\n  - Field names are given an ID/tag. Hence field names can be renamed . Tag number cannot be changed.\n  - Field data type is also ENCODED INTO the binary format .field datatyepe in some cases can be changed.\n  - required, optional mentioned in the schema definition , hence enforced at only runtime , it is not encoded in BYTES\n        - if the field value is not set, then it is not encoded in bytes. \n  - Thrift has two different encoding regular and compact\n  - READERs vs WRITERs Schema is not part of PROTOBUF or thrift or JSON, But confluent schema registry is designed based on that\n  \n ",
			"rawText": "Thrift, Protobuf:\n  - Field names are given an ID/tag. Hence field names can be renamed . Tag number cannot be changed.\n  - Field data type is also ENCODED INTO the binary format .field datatyepe in some cases can be changed.\n  - required, optional mentioned in the schema definition , hence enforced at only runtime , it is not encoded in BYTES\n        - if the field value is not set, then it is not encoded in bytes. \n  - Thrift has two different encoding regular and compact\n  - READERs vs WRITERs Schema is not part of PROTOBUF or thrift or JSON, But confluent schema registry is designed based on that\n  \n ",
			"fontSize": 16.063917631513828,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Thrift, Protobuf:\n  - Field names are given an ID/tag. Hence field names can be renamed . Tag number cannot be changed.\n  - Field data type is also ENCODED INTO the binary format .field datatyepe in some cases can be changed.\n  - required, optional mentioned in the schema definition , hence enforced at only runtime , it is not encoded in BYTES\n        - if the field value is not set, then it is not encoded in bytes. \n  - Thrift has two different encoding regular and compact\n  - READERs vs WRITERs Schema is not part of PROTOBUF or thrift or JSON, But confluent schema registry is designed based on that\n  \n ",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25
		},
		{
			"id": "gzWynghU",
