			"type": "text",
			"x": 7177.848286930251,
			"y": 711.4334911016226,
			"width": 1117.614990234375,
			"height": 140,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bDO",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 457714839,
			"version": 915,
			"versionNonce": 58539161,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773093183483,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "AVRO\n  - Field names are not encoded binary format, field data types, required , optional are also not  encoded in binary format.\n  - To construct data, use a schema  DEFN to read field name, and read binary data to assign value to field\n    Binary data can only be decoded correctly  if the code reading the data is using the same exact schema as the code that wrote the data.\n    Any mismatch  in the schema between the reader and the writer would mean incorrectly decoded data.\n-  AVRO Doensn't have OPTIONAL & Required markers\n- ADDING both WRITER & READER to each record  will add to the DATA storage cost, SCHME size is higher than data size",
			"rawText": "AVRO\n  - Field names are not encoded binary format, field data types, required , optional are also not  encoded in binary format.\n  - To construct data, use a schema  DEFN to read field name, and read binary data to assign value to field\n    Binary data can only be decoded correctly  if the code reading the data is using the same exact schema as the code that wrote the data.\n    Any mismatch  in the schema between the reader and the writer would mean incorrectly decoded data.\n-  AVRO Doensn't have OPTIONAL & Required markers\n- ADDING both WRITER & READER to each record  will add to the DATA storage cost, SCHME size is higher than data size",
			"fontSize": 16,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "AVRO\n  - Field names are not encoded binary format, field data types, required , optional are also not  encoded in binary format.\n  - To construct data, use a schema  DEFN to read field name, and read binary data to assign value to field\n    Binary data can only be decoded correctly  if the code reading the data is using the same exact schema as the code that wrote the data.\n    Any mismatch  in the schema between the reader and the writer would mean incorrectly decoded data.\n-  AVRO Doensn't have OPTIONAL & Required markers\n- ADDING both WRITER & READER to each record  will add to the DATA storage cost, SCHME size is higher than data size",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25
		},
		{
			"id": "Gkbbj0BF",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 7188.361176386339,
			"y": 856.6967596536559,
			"width": 941.0847778320312,
			"height": 215.4718517338577,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bDQ",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1767014425,
			"version": 1245,
			"versionNonce": 120610775,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773093185205,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "WRITER's schema & Reader's schema ( Baked into AVRO by default  & Confluent SR is based on this concept)\n- IMPORTANT: \n   IN AVRO , WRITER's schema & Reader's schema doesnt have to be the same\n   - The schema's only have to be compatible\n   A READER's SCHEMA also needs WRITERS schema to check the field Names & data type.\n        - if a new field is added in Reader's it should have a default value.\n       WRITER's SCHEMA:\n           HADOOP world:  Large file with  lots of records ( millions) with a single schema,  in the beginnig\n          \n",
			"rawText": "WRITER's schema & Reader's schema ( Baked into AVRO by default  & Confluent SR is based on this concept)\n- IMPORTANT: \n   IN AVRO , WRITER's schema & Reader's schema doesnt have to be the same\n   - The schema's only have to be compatible\n   A READER's SCHEMA also needs WRITERS schema to check the field Names & data type.\n        - if a new field is added in Reader's it should have a default value.\n       WRITER's SCHEMA:\n           HADOOP world:  Large file with  lots of records ( millions) with a single schema,  in the beginnig\n          \n",
			"fontSize": 17.237748138708618,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "WRITER's schema & Reader's schema ( Baked into AVRO by default  & Confluent SR is based on this concept)\n- IMPORTANT: \n   IN AVRO , WRITER's schema & Reader's schema doesnt have to be the same\n   - The schema's only have to be compatible\n   A READER's SCHEMA also needs WRITERS schema to check the field Names & data type.\n        - if a new field is added in Reader's it should have a default value.\n       WRITER's SCHEMA:\n           HADOOP world:  Large file with  lots of records ( millions) with a single schema,  in the beginnig\n          \n",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25
		},
